{
  "name": "Add each day's new matches of a saved search to a list and a campaign",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Add each day's new matches of a saved search to a list and a campaign\n\n### How it works\nKeep a campaign fed with fresh people, on a budget. Every morning the workflow runs your saved search again and adds only the new matches to a list; people already in it are skipped. When the number of new people is within max_new_per_day, the list goes into your campaign, where only valid emails join and people taken out earlier stay out. Above the budget, nothing is spent and Slack tells you how many are waiting.\n\nCosts: the list is free; the campaign add costs 1 credit per new person.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Save a search as a list in Argorant (your filters), and create a second list as the target.\n4. Pick both in **Add new matches to the list**, and the campaign in **Add the list to the campaign**.\n5. Set max_new_per_day in **Settings**, add a Slack credential and activate.\n\n### Customization\nChange the time in **Every day at 7:00** or send the over budget note by email.",
        "height": 626,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
